# Violations of tooling/conformance/integrity.ts that are known and owned.
# One per line: project<TAB>rule<TAB>subject<TAB>why. The subject is the
# violation's text, except under cascade-has-root, where it is the blamed
# cause: one entry per unrecorded root, covering every cascade through it;
# and under top-level-cut, where it is what was cut: `the initializer of G`,
# `a statement calling C`, or `module#init`. The cut entries are the ratchet
# toward `nts build` refusing a cut: the day none is left, it can.
# A generic statement cut is named `a statement at <file>:<line>:<column>`;
# files are project-relative, or repository-relative for imported dependencies.
# Under location-on-a-token the subject is the diagnostic code: one cause (a
# node's full start used for its token start), so a project names it once.
# Closure numbers and type ids are normalised (ClosureN, <N>, objN). An entry
# that no longer occurs is reported for removal; any violation not listed
# here fails. Entries are in byte order (LC_ALL=C sort), and integrity.ts
# enforces it: insert a new entry where it sorts, never at the end.
